         "A <b>transistor</b> is a tap with an electric handle. A tiny trickle into the base opens a much bigger flow from collector to emitter. Used one way it is an <b>amplifier</b> (copy a small wiggle into a large one). Used the other it is a <b>switch</b> (fully on or fully off), and billions of switches make a computer chip.",
         "An <b>op-amp</b> is a very sensitive amplifier with two inputs: it pushes its output as hard as it can to make the two inputs equal. Add feedback and you can tame it to amplify by an exact amount, or compare two voltages and say which is bigger.",
